## Context

**High priority.** The effectiveness batch assembled during the Gavard & Schoch
audit (see 0704, section Upstream material) feeds controversy 2 of the REL
review. It must also serve as the basis for the measure-coding table, then for
the reproducibility audit (0863). REL deadline: 2026-12-06.
Three texts were missing. The published version of Gavard & Schoch (2026) was
obtained on 2026-09-13 by writing to the authors: that is the route that works.
It is in `~/CNRS/papiers/actif/Gavard Scotch 2026 Climate finance counterproductive/2609-PublishedVersion.pdf`.

Two texts remain, both of favourable sign. They must be read: methodological
critique has to be symmetric, and a batch made only of unfavourable results
would be biased.

- **Wang, L. & Tang, J. (2026).** « From Climate Finance to Sustainable
  Development: The Synergy of Financial Instruments and National Governance for
  Achieving SDG 13. » *Sustainable Development*, Early View.
  https://doi.org/10.1002/sd.70738. Double machine learning, 171 countries,
  2013–2023. It is the only text in the batch after the 2013 break in MDB
  reporting.
- **Zeng, A. et al. (2022).** « The impact of climate aid on carbon emissions
  reduction and the role of renewable energy: evidence from Belt and Road
  countries. » *Environmental Science and Pollution Research* 29, 77401–77417.
  https://doi.org/10.1007/s11356-022-21185-y

## Relevant files

- `~/CNRS/papiers/actif/Gavard Scotch 2026 Climate finance counterproductive/docs/`: PDF staging (EDM discipline, outside the repository)
- same folder, `docs/missing-papers.html`: status list, to be updated
- same folder, `correspondence/request-published-pdf-2026-09-11.md`: request template that succeeded

## Actions

1. Identify the corresponding author of each article and a current address
   (the previous request bounced twice on outdated addresses: check the
   institutional page before sending).
2. Draft the two requests on the model of 11 September. The author sends them.
3. In parallel: try institutional access and an author version
   (HAL, ResearchGate, institutional repository).
4. On receipt: PDF into staging `docs/`, Zotero import, `missing-papers.html` updated.

## Verification

- [ ] Two PDFs present in staging and in Zotero
- [ ] `missing-papers.html` no longer lists any pending text

## Exit criteria

- Both full texts are available, or the impossibility is documented
  after a follow-up unanswered at fifteen days.
